# SHA-256 of the output of `lake env ./.lake/build/bin/statementpin`: the
# elaborated form of the frozen vocabulary (PLAN M8.a accept gate, step 1).
#
# NOT CANDIDATE MATERIAL. A weakened statement -- an added hypothesis on
# `VerifierCorrect`, a dropped conjunct in `Represents`, a widened frame, a
# moved input address, a redefined hash `ECALL` -- builds cleanly, passes the
# axiom sweep, passes every fixture, and scores better. This hash is the only
# thing in the gate that catches it.
#
# `verifier`, `verifierCode` and every index derived from the region lengths
# are deliberately NOT in the pinned set: those are what a candidate changes.
# See `XmssAsmTools/StatementPin.lean` for the list and why each name is on it.
#
# Re-pinning is a human action in its own commit. The legitimate reason is a
# toolchain bump moving the pretty-printer's output with no change in meaning;
# diff the two dumps before believing that.
6d88a00e07b8bca095e4be00ca72525d2ec6bb4144a64a0532b3841dd7b28f03
